trixie: use mesa-libclc (build/mesa-libclc.yaml) in place of libclc-19.
Mesa prefers mesa-libclc. libclc-19 is old upstream libclc: it has no
fixes for tgamma and __clc_flush_denormal_if_not_supported.
mesa-opencl-icd loads the SPIR-V files at run time, so it depends on it.
rusticl also needs the OpenCL C headers of clang at run time
(opencl-c-base.h). libclc-19 gave them through libclang-common-19-dev.
Change control.in too: the clean step makes control again from control.in.

